# In dev, vite.config.ts proxies /api to http://localhost:8000 - point that
# at a running engine/api server (see engine/Dockerfile, or the no-spend
# dev server under engine/api/dev_server.py).

# Read-aloud step 1 (lib/flags.ts). Only the literal string "on" turns it
# on - unset, empty, or anything else stays off. Copy this file to
# .env.local (gitignored) and uncomment to test locally. No deploy config
# currently wires this through at all: engine/Dockerfile's frontend-build
# stage runs `npm run build` with no ARG/ENV for it, so setting this in
# Render's dashboard or render.yaml would have no effect on what actually
# ships - turning it on for real users needs a deliberate Dockerfile +
# render.yaml change first (Build/Ministry/Technology/
# CiC_ReadAloud_Step1_Design_Note.md), not made yet.
# VITE_READ_ALOUD=on

# Same story for the Conversation Transparency Engine's own flag - also
# unset everywhere, also not wired into the Docker build
# (Build/Ministry/Features/Conversation-Transparency-Engine/Decision-Log.md,
# Entry 41: "no deployment config currently sets
# VITE_TRANSPARENCY_ANCHOR_RENDERER at all... flipping it later is a
# deploy-config change, not a code change"). Listed here for the same
# local-testing reason, not touched or owned by this file's edit.
# VITE_TRANSPARENCY_ANCHOR_RENDERER=on
